	"notes": "A List Apart is a blog, and it reads like one: everything lives in a single column that never gets wider than 960px, no matter how wide the browser is — extra space just becomes bigger side margins. The only place it truly divides into more than one column is a small strip further down, 'More from A List Apart', where three article summaries sit side by side as equal cards; that strip falls back to one column on a narrow screen, same as everywhere else. A small ad box floats beside the top two articles on a desktop, but the scan tool never found it because it has no landmark role — a reminder that a screenshot can show something the CSS scan misses entirely. On a phone the header's four text links are replaced by a single hamburger button.",
